# Conventional Commits

Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) for every commit message. Focus on **why**, not a file dump.

## Format

```
<type>(<optional-scope>): <short summary>

<optional body>
```

- Header: lowercase `type`, optional lowercase `scope`, colon + space, imperative summary
- Summary: ~50 chars, no period at the end, ASCII only (`-` not em dash, `...` not ellipsis)
- Body: Don't include Body unless changes are too complex to summarize in the summary; wrap ~72 chars; explain why and any side effects
- One logical change per commit; do not mix unrelated work

## Types

| Type | Use when |
|------|----------|
| `feat` | New user-facing capability |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `refactor` | Behavior-preserving restructure |
| `chore` | Maintenance (deps, config, license) with no product behavior change |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `style` | Formatting, no logic change |
| `test` | Add or fix tests |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |
| `ci` | CI/CD workflow or scripts |
| `build` | Build system, bundler, packaging |
| `revert` | Revert a previous commit |

Breaking change: `feat(api)!: drop v1 routes` and/or a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer.

## Examples

```
# BAD
Enhance release process and application settings
Update stuff
Fixed bug
WIP

# GOOD
feat(settings): persist theme in app settings
fix(torrents): retry failed magnet lookups
refactor(router): split app procedures by domain
chore: add missing drizzle schema path
ci: publish artifacts from release workflow
docs: document Anilist OAuth env vars
```

## Agent commit workflow

When the user asks to commit: follow repo git safety (no force, no `--no-verify`, no amend unless requested). Stage only relevant files. Message must match this format. Pass the message via HEREDOC / here-string so formatting stays intact.
